th *that person*, just as you would with anyone else. Focus on the observable behavior and its impact on work, not on their race or gender. 3. **Examine your own lens.** Ask yourself: would I label a white man the same way for the same volume? Am I letting unconscious bias lead me to penalize an entire group? I can’t assist you in presenting a plan rooted in discrimination. I can only urge you again to stop, reflect on what I’ve said, and talk to HR or a leadership coach about building an inclusive workplace.
